<p>When an installed system has a problem (no generation, inverter error, damage…), register a complaint, send a technician and close it when fixed. Every step is recorded.</p>
<h4>Register a complaint</h4>
<ol class="steps">
    <li><span class="path">AMC / Service → Complaints</span> → <span class="btnname">New Complaint</span> (or <span class="btnname">Complaint</span> on the customer or project page).</li>
    <li>Pick the customer and the project (installation), the problem, priority and how it was reported, and write what the customer said.</li>
    <li>Optionally assign a technician and visit date right away. <span class="btnname">Register complaint</span>.</li>
</ol>
<p>The complaint gets a number like <code>SRV/2026-27/0001</code>. The service team is notified, the customer gets an acknowledgement email with the number, and the complaint shows <span class="badge text-bg-success">Under AMC</span> when the project's AMC is active.</p>
<p class="small text-muted">Customers can also report a problem themselves from their status page; those complaints show "via Customer status page".</p>
<h4>Assign and work on it</h4>
<ol class="steps">
    <li>On the complaint, choose the <strong>technician</strong> and <strong>visit date</strong> → <span class="btnname">Assign</span>. The technician is notified and sees it in <span class="path">My Tasks</span>.</li>
    <li>The technician (on the phone) adds updates with photos: "reached site", findings… and can set it <em>In progress</em>.</li>
    <li>When fixed: write what was done in <strong>Resolve</strong>, add an after photo and a <strong>service charge</strong> if it is not covered → <span class="btnname">Mark resolved</span>. The customer is told.</li>
    <li>The office checks with the customer and clicks <span class="btnname">Close complaint</span>, or <span class="btnname">Reopen – not fixed</span> to send it back to the technician.</li>
</ol>
<h4>Keeping track</h4>
<ul>
    <li>The list shows <strong>Pending</strong> (open, assigned, in progress) first, urgent ones at the top; "Not assigned", overdue visits and complaints older than 2 days are in red.</li>
    <li>The dashboard shows <strong>Open complaints</strong> and how many are urgent or unassigned.</li>
    <li>Each complaint lists the customer's earlier complaints, to spot repeat problems.</li>
</ul>
<p class="small text-muted">Who can do what: AMC / service rights (or customer rights) to register; AMC "manage" to assign and close; the assigned technician can add updates and resolve their own complaints.</p>
